tests: give the keys with no array type a valid gguf_type in test-gguf
Fold-into: upstream/ggml

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

get_kv_types of test-gguf gives each key that is not an array the element
type gguf_type(-1). enum gguf_type has no fixed underlying type, and its
values are 0 to 13, thus -1 is not in the range of the enum. UBSan reports
an invalid-enum-load in std::make_pair in get_kv_types, in debug and
release, for each seed.

The change: the placeholder is GGUF_TYPE_COUNT, a valid value of the enum
that is not a type. The test reads the element type only for an array key,
and it compares it with GGUF_TYPE_STRING for the other keys, thus the
handcrafted files and the random sequence do not change. Test code only.

diff --git a/tests/test-gguf.cpp b/tests/test-gguf.cpp
index fc63618..4b4e8b8 100644
--- a/tests/test-gguf.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-gguf.cpp
@@ -155,7 +155,9 @@ static std::vector<std::pair<enum gguf_type, enum gguf_type>> get_kv_types(std::
             continue;
         }
 
-        kv_types.push_back(std::make_pair(type, gguf_type(-1)));
+        // No element type. The value must be in the range of the enum: -1 is not, and a load of
+        // it is undefined behavior.
+        kv_types.push_back(std::make_pair(type, GGUF_TYPE_COUNT));
     }
     std::shuffle(kv_types.begin(), kv_types.end(), rng);
 
